### 4. Visible Faults & Technical Issues

* **Absurd Object Hallucination (00:52–00:57):** The biggest blunder in the cut. In Andersen's tale, the *roast goose* (stuffed with apples and prunes, with a knife and fork in its back) waddles toward her. Here, the AI generator spawned a **live white farm goose** hopping off the table right in front of the still-plated roast goose, complete with loud live-goose honking on the soundtrack. It turns a poignant starving hallucination into unintended comedy.
* **Backwards Carriage & Phantom Slipper (00:10–00:13):** In Shot 3, the carriage on the left is driving *backwards* up the street while the carriage on the right drives forward. Meanwhile, the girl is already barefoot on the left pavement while a giant slipper materializes out of nowhere in the center of the street and flips toward the camera.
* **Missing Lip-Sync (00:16–00:18, 01:10–01:11, 01:26–01:28, 01:49–01:51):**
  * At **00:16–00:18**, the girl says *"Matches... who will buy my matches?"* (two phrases), but her mouth only opens once briefly at 00:16 and is closed for the second half of her line.
  * At **01:10**, **01:26**, and **01:49**, characters speak dialogue over completely frozen still images with zero mouth movement.
* **Unstruck Matches (00:34–00:35, 01:14–01:15):** In Shot 8, the match simply self-ignites in mid-air without scraping the wall despite the loud strike SFX. At 01:12–01:15, she holds an unlit match in Shot 17, and in Shot 18 it is suddenly lit without a strike or narrative cue (before she strikes the "fourth" match at 01:20, messing up the match count!).
* **Stove Doesn't Vanish (00:44–00:45):** When the narrator says *"Then it went out"* and the match extinguishes into smoke, the giant iron stove remains solidly in the snow rather than disappearing.
* **Unwanted Watercolor Vignette Border (01:15–01:19):** Shot 18 has rough white unpainted paper edges framing the image, breaking the full-bleed framing of every other shot in the film.

